# A classroom lesson plan authored as document code.
output = ARGV.len() > 0 ? ARGV[0] : "markdown-lesson-plan.docx"; let body = """---
title: Lesson Plan - Water in a Changing Climate
author: Rowan Bell, Cedar Valley School
theme: business
page_size: letter
---
# Water in a Changing Climate

**Grade 7 science** · 55 minutes · Rowan Bell

## Learning goals

By the end of the lesson, students will be able to explain how evaporation and runoff move water through a watershed and support one claim with evidence.

## Materials

- Two clear cups and ice
- Watershed diagram and colored pencils
- Exit ticket

## Sequence

| Minutes | Activity | Evidence |
| ---: | :--- | :--- |
| 0-8 | Notice and wonder | Student questions |
| 8-20 | Mini-lesson | Annotated diagram |
| 20-42 | Model a watershed | Partner explanation |
| 42-55 | Exit ticket | One claim and evidence |

## Teacher notes

> Invite students to distinguish what they observe from what they infer. Offer sentence frames to multilingual learners.

```text
Water falls -> collects -> flows -> evaporates -> condenses
```

## Assessment

Students who name two connected processes and cite the model meet the objective. Collect unfinished diagrams for the next conference.
""";
# host dependency: cli="lmoffice docx" install="github:lmctl-ai/lmoffice@v0.1.31"
schema_p = load_schema(schema="../schema/docx.dsl.json");
p = _lmcode_ schema_p;
let d=docx.create(${output}); d.markdown(${body}).save();
end _lmcode_
r = run_lmcode(p, {command:["lmoffice","docx","--lmcode","$DSLFILE"]}); assert(r.ok);
